Class Struggles and the Revolutionary Party is a seminal work by Italian Marxist theorist Arrigo Cervetto that examines the role of class struggle in shaping revolutionary political organization. The text provides a critical analysis of traditional party structures, advocating instead for a dynamic, class-based approach to revolutionary mobilization. Written against the backdrop of mid‑20th‑century political theory, Cervetto's work has influenced debates on party reform and revolutionary strategy, offering both theoretical insights and practical guidelines for organizing the working class.
